<section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>What Is a Smoke Exhaust Unit?</h2></div><p class="fcx-lead">A smoke exhaust unit is a mechanical ventilation system designed to extract smoke and hot gases from a building during a fire. It usually works as part of a larger smoke management system and is connected to the required exhaust or duct arrangement.</p><p class="fcx-lead">The main purpose of <b>Smoke Exhaust Units in Delhi</b> is to help remove smoke from specific areas during an emergency. This can help maintain better visibility and support evacuation by reducing the concentration of smoke and hot gases in occupied areas.</p><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--2"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fire"></i></span><h3>High-Temperature Smoke Exhaust Fans</h3><p>Smoke exhaust systems require fans that may continue operating under elevated temperature conditions for the specified period. The Delhi range includes fire-rated configurations designed for 300°C / 400°C for two hours, depending on the selected unit.</p><p>These high-temperature options are intended for emergency smoke extraction applications where the fan needs to handle hot gases during a fire scenario.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fire"></i></span><h3>Insulated Smoke Exhaust Construction</h3><p>The smoke exhaust units are equipped with double-skin insulated casings. This construction provides a suitable enclosure for the fan and supports the requirements of smoke extraction systems.</p><p>Automatic control systems also can be incorporated into the overall arrangement to help operate the smoke extraction equipment during an emergency, depending on the project design.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Key Features of Smoke Exhaust Units</h2><p>Smoke Exhaust Units can be designed for different building and industrial requirements. Important features include:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>High-temperature fire-rated fan options</li><li>Smoke and hot gas extraction</li><li>Double-skin insulated casing</li><li>Automatic control system options</li><li>Different fan sizes and capacities</li><li>Suitable for emergency ventilation</li><li>Designed for high-temperature operation</li><li>Suitable for industrial and commercial buildings</li><li>Available for basement and high-rise applications</li><li>Selection based on airflow and static pressure</li></ul><p>The current Delhi product range covers fan sizes from 315 mm to 1000 mm, with capacity up to 40,000 CFM and static pressure up to 80 mmWG.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><div class="fcx-spec"><table class="fcx-table"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Product</th><td>Smoke Exhaust Unit</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Size Range</th><td>315 mm to 1000 mm</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Capacity</th><td>Up to 40,000 CFM</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Static Pressure</th><td>Up to 80 mmWG</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Fire Rating</th><td>300°C / 400°C for 2 Hours</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Casing</th><td>Double-Skin Insulated</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Main Function</th><td>Smoke &amp; Hot Gas Extraction</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Control</th><td>Automatic Control System Options</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Applications</th><td>Malls, Basements, High-Rise Buildings, Factories</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="fcx-note"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-sliders"></i></span><div><p>The specific configuration should be selected according to the required airflow, static pressure, building design, operating conditions, and overall fire-safety design.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Applications of Smoke Exhaust Units</h2></div><p class="fcx-lead">Industrial Smoke Exhaust Units and building smoke extraction systems may be used in various places where smoke management is required.</p><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--3"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-square-parking"></i></span><h3>Basement Parking Areas</h3><p>Basements and underground parking areas can fill with smoke quickly during a fire due to their enclosed nature. Smoke exhaust units can be incorporated into the ventilation system to extract smoke and hot gases through designated exhaust routes.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-people-group"></i></span><h3>Shopping Malls</h3><p>Large shopping malls contain high-occupancy areas and enclosed areas. Smoke extraction systems may be integrated into the building's fire-safety design to help control smoke during an emergency.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-building"></i></span><h3>High-Rise Buildings</h3><p>High-rise buildings require carefully planned fire and smoke management systems. Smoke exhaust units can be used in suitable areas to support smoke extraction and emergency ventilation.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-building"></i></span><h3>Factories and Industrial Buildings</h3><p>Industrial facilities may also contain large enclosed manufacturing and storage areas. Smoke exhaust systems can be integrated into the ventilation and fire-safety arrangement according to the building design.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-hospital"></i></span><h3>Hospitals and Hotels</h3><p>Hospitals, hotels, and other occupied buildings also can require dedicated smoke management systems. A properly designed smoke exhaust system can form part of the overall emergency ventilation strategy.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-duo"><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fire"></i></span><h2>Benefits of Smoke Exhaust Units</h2><p>One of the main benefits of smoke exhaust units is their ability to remove smoke and hot gases from different areas during a fire emergency. This can help improve visibility and support safer movement through the building.</p><p>Fire-rated fan configurations are designed to function under high-temperature conditions for the specified period. This makes them suitable for applications where normal ventilation fans might not be appropriate for emergency smoke extraction.</p><p>Another advantage is the availability of different sizes and capacities. This allows the equipment to be selected according to the airflow and pressure requirements of the building.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fire"></i></span><h2>Smoke Exhaust Unit Suppliers in Delhi</h2><p>Choosing suitable <b>Smoke Exhaust Unit Suppliers in Delhi</b> is critical because smoke extraction performance depends on correct equipment selection and system design. The fan needs to be selected according to the required airflow, static pressure, temperature rating, and installation conditions.</p><p>The current Delhi product data state that each unit is chosen according to the required airflow, static pressure, and site conditions. Technical sizing and information can be supplied before ordering, while the completed equipment can be dispatched to Delhi and other places throughout India.</p><p>For Delhi NCR projects, the manufacturing facility at Neemrana, Rajasthan, is located on the Delhi-Jaipur Highway (NH-48), providing convenient access for projects across the region.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel" style="grid-column:1/-1"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fire"></i></span><h2>Smoke Exhaust Unit Manufacturer in India</h2><p>A reliable <b>Smoke Exhaust Unit Manufacturer in India</b> should provide units suitable for different building sizes and emergency ventilation requirements. Proper fan selection is critical because the smoke extraction system needs to fit the building's airflow, pressure, temperature, and fire-protection requirements.</p><p>Manufacturers should also offer technical data for correct sizing and integration with the building's smoke control system. The final selection needs to be made according to the complete project design rather than only the physical size of the fan.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>How to Choose the Right Smoke Exhaust Unit?</h2><p>Before selecting a smoke exhaust unit, consider the following factors:</p><ul class="fcx-checks fcx-checks--long"><li><b>Airflow requirement:</b> Determine the required CFM for the smoke extraction system.</li><li><b>Static pressure:</b> Consider duct resistance and other system components.</li><li><b>Temperature rating:</b> Select the suitable fire-rated configuration for the application.</li><li><b>Building type:</b> Consider whether the unit will be used in a basement, mall, factory, high-rise, hospital, or hotel.</li><li><b>Installation area:</b> Check the available space and duct arrangement.</li><li><b>Control system:</b> Consider how the fan can be activated during an emergency.</li><li><b>Site conditions:</b> Review the whole installation environment before the final selection.</li></ul><p>Correct sizing and system planning are essential for achieving the specified smoke extraction performance.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>FAQs</h2></div><div class="fcx-faq"><details><summary>What is a smoke exhaust unit used for?</summary><p>A smoke exhaust unit is used to remove smoke and hot toxic gases from buildings during a fire emergency. It can help maintain visibility and support safer evacuation.</p></details><details><summary>What is the capacity of the smoke exhaust units?</summary><p>The current Delhi range has a capacity of up to 40,000 CFM, depending on the selected configuration.</p></details><details><summary>What size smoke exhaust units are available?</summary><p>The listed size range is 315 mm to 1000 mm. The appropriate size depends on the airflow and static pressure requirements of the project.</p></details><details><summary>Are fire-rated smoke exhaust units available?</summary><p>Yes. The Delhi product page lists fire-rated configurations for 300°C / 400°C for two hours, depending on the selected unit.</p></details><details><summary>Where are smoke exhaust units normally used?</summary><p>Smoke exhaust units are usually used in basements, department stores, high-rise buildings, factories, hospitals, hotels, and other buildings where emergency smoke extraction is needed.</p></details></div><div class="fcx-center" style="margin-top:26px"><a href="product.php" class="btn-cyber btn-cyber--primary fcx-btn" title="Fan Air India Products">Learn More <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-cta"><h2>Conclusion</h2><p><b>Smoke Exhaust Unit Manufacturers in Delhi</b> provide emergency ventilation systems designed to remove smoke and hot gases from buildings during fire conditions. With sizes from 315 mm to 1000 mm, capacities up to 40,000 CFM, static pressure up to 80 mmWG, and fire-rated options for 300°C / 400°C for 2 hours, the system can be selected according to different project requirements.</p><p>FanAir India Pvt. Ltd. supplies smoke exhaust units for Delhi NCR and projects throughout India, with technical sizing based on airflow, static pressure, application, and location conditions.</p><a href="../contact.php" class="fcx-cta__btn" title="Contact Fan Air India">Contact Us <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section>
